  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nWeak low pressure is noted in the convergent low cloud field across\nnorthern Ohio early this afternoon. High-res guidance shows a\nconvergent axis shifting slowly south through evening bringing an\nincreasing chance of showers and storms across parts of central Ohio.\n\nMeanwhile, slightly higher instability along with another weak\nboundary will provide higher chances of convection from northern\nKentucky through south-central Ohio. Could see gusty winds and \nlocally heavy rain in this area due to the deep moisture noted on \nmodel soundings. Activity will decrease around sunset.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2). \nWeak mid-level troughing will persist across the middle Ohio Valley\nthrough Wednesday with isolated storms possible each day (especially\nacross our southern counties). Late in the week, a passing shortwave\ndropping southeast through the Great Lakes will bring a frontal\nboundary and a additional thunderstorm chances late Thursday and\nFriday.",
